# What the build context excludes. The Dockerfile copies explicit paths, so this is
# defence in depth plus speed: a secret never enters the daemon's context, and the
# context is small enough that a build does not start by uploading node_modules.

# Secrets and environment.
.env
.env.*
*.env
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
secrets/
.secrets/

# Reproducible, local, or somebody's tooling.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.tsbuild
dist
coverage
.git
.github
.claude
.DS_Store

# Not part of the API image. The web client contributes only its manifest, which the
# lockfile needs to validate.
apps/web/*
!apps/web/package.json
docs
scripts
docker
docker-compose*.yml
*.md

# Tests and what only tests use stay out of the image that runs in production: 75 test files
# were shipped, and code that exists to forge a signed-in user and a database that must not
# be touched has no business in an image. (Lint refuses production code importing the
# test-only directory, so nothing the process loads is among them; the smoke test would
# fail if it were.)
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
apps/api/src/testing

# The demo seeder makes people with live sessions and writes their cookies to a file. It is a
# development tool (`bun run demo`), guarded by the name of the database it will write to, and
# kept out of the image so that no container can run it at all (H-API 9).
apps/api/src/cli/demo-*.ts
apps/api/src/cli/seed-demo.ts
